IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc1-common`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 2, entitlement: the introduction (regulation 7), the financial
-- conditions (regulations 17 and 18) and the restrictions on entitlement (regulations 19 and 19A).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- The basic conditions (section 4) and the financial conditions (section 5) are the Act's, which is not among the inputs: the
-- minimum amount and the capital limit are named by these regulations, and "meets the basic conditions" is a plain input.
-- What counts as a person's capital is Part 6 (piece uc2): the capital arrives as a number.
-- Money is a NUMBER of pounds.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 7 only introduces the Part: it lists the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act (regulations 8 to 16), the financial
-- conditions in section 5 (regulations 17 and 18) and "cases where no entitlement arises even if the basic conditions and the financial
-- conditions are met" (regulation 19). The rule joins the three subjects: entitlement can arise where the basic and the financial
-- conditions are met and no restriction in regulation 19 applies. The "only if" is read from the last limb and from regulation 19(1);
-- the words of regulation 7 do not say it, and the Act (out of range) states the entitlement conditions (fork F-7-JOIN, assumed and not ruled).
-- src:181 | This Part contains provisions about—
-- src:182 | (a) the requirement to meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act, including exceptions from that requirement;
-- src:183 | (b) the maximum amount of capital and the minimum amount of universal credit for the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act; and
-- src:184 | (c) cases where no entitlement to universal credit arises even if the basic conditions and the financial conditions are met.
@ref reg 7 (src:181-184)
GIVEN `the person meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
      `the person meets the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
      `regulation 19 prevents entitlement from arising` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7 — entitlement to universal credit can arise` `the person meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` `the person meets the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act` `regulation 19 prevents entitlement from arising` MEANS
    (`the person meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act`)
    AND (`the person meets the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act`)
    AND (NOT `regulation 19 prevents entitlement from arising`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 17: the minimum amount is one penny.
-- src:401 | For the purposes of section 5(1)(b) and (2)(b) of the Act (financial conditions: amount payable not less than any prescribed minimum) the minimum is one penny.
@ref reg 17 (src:401)
`reg 17 — the minimum amount` MEANS 0.01

-- The financial condition of section 5(1)(b) and (2)(b): the amount payable is not less than the minimum.
-- src:401 | For the purposes of section 5(1)(b) and (2)(b) of the Act (financial conditions: amount payable not less than any prescribed minimum) the minimum is one penny.
@ref reg 17 (src:401)
GIVEN `amount payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 17 — the amount payable is not less than the minimum` `amount payable` MEANS
    `amount payable` AT LEAST `reg 17 — the minimum amount`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 18: capital limit.

-- (1) The prescribed amount is £16,000 for a single claimant and £16,000 for joint claimants.
-- src:403 | (1) For the purposes of section 5(1)(a) and (2)(a) of the Act (financial conditions: capital limit)—
-- src:404 | (a) the prescribed amount for a single claimant is £16,000; and
-- src:405 | (b) the prescribed amount for joint claimants is £16,000.
@ref reg 18(1) (src:403-405)
GIVEN `claim basis` IS A `Claim basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18(1) — the prescribed capital amount` `claim basis` MEANS
    CONSIDER `claim basis`
    WHEN `a single claimant` THEN 16000
    WHEN `joint claimants` THEN 16000
    WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` THEN 16000

-- (2) Where the claimant is a member of a couple but claims as a single person, their capital is treated as including the capital of
-- the other member. For joint claimants the capital that section 5(2) of the Act measures is that of the two together (fork
-- F-18-JOINT, assumed and not ruled: the Act is not among the inputs).
-- src:406 | (2) In a case where the claimant is a member of a couple, but makes a claim as a single person, the claimant's capital is to be treated as including the capital of the other member of the couple.
@ref reg 18(2) (src:406)
GIVEN `claim basis` IS A `Claim basis`
      `the claimant's capital` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: Part 6 (piece uc2)
      `the capital of the other member of the couple` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: Part 6 (piece uc2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18(2) — the capital taken into account` `claim basis` `the claimant's capital` `the capital of the other member of the couple` MEANS
    CONSIDER `claim basis`
    WHEN `a single claimant` THEN `the claimant's capital`
    WHEN `joint claimants` THEN `the claimant's capital` PLUS `the capital of the other member of the couple`
    WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` THEN `the claimant's capital` PLUS `the capital of the other member of the couple`

-- The financial condition of section 5(1)(a) and (2)(a): the capital is not more than the prescribed amount ("the maximum amount of
-- capital", as regulation 7(b) puts it).
-- src:183 | (b) the maximum amount of capital and the minimum amount of universal credit for the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act; and
-- src:403 | (1) For the purposes of section 5(1)(a) and (2)(a) of the Act (financial conditions: capital limit)—
-- src:404 | (a) the prescribed amount for a single claimant is £16,000; and
-- src:405 | (b) the prescribed amount for joint claimants is £16,000.
@ref reg 18(1) (src:183-405)
GIVEN `claim basis` IS A `Claim basis`
      `capital taken into account` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: Part 6 (piece uc2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(1) — the capital is within the limit` `claim basis` `capital taken into account` MEANS
    `capital taken into account` AT MOST (`reg 18(1) — the prescribed capital amount` `claim basis`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 19: restrictions on entitlement.

-- (4) "Serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital": (a) being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act
-- 1983 before the day the Secretary of State certifies to be the person's release date (where there is one); or (b) being detained under
-- section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003.
-- src:417 | (4) In paragraph (1)(c) a person serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital is a person who is—
-- src:418 | (a) being detained—
-- src:419 | (i) under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (power of higher courts to direct hospital admission; removal to hospital of persons serving sentence of imprisonment etc), and
-- src:420 | (ii) before the day which the Secretary of State certifies to be that person's release date within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act (in any case where there is such a release date); or
-- src:421 | (b) being detained under—
-- src:422 | (i) section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction), or
-- src:423 | (ii) section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder).
@ref reg 19(4) (src:417-423)
DECLARE `Person who may be serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` HAS
    `the person is being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on detention in hospital (not a piece)
    `release date that the Secretary of State certifies, within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act`  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on detention in hospital (not a piece)
    `the person is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on detention in hospital (not a piece)

-- src:417 | (4) In paragraph (1)(c) a person serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital is a person who is—
-- src:418 | (a) being detained—
-- src:419 | (i) under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (power of higher courts to direct hospital admission; removal to hospital of persons serving sentence of imprisonment etc), and
-- src:420 | (ii) before the day which the Secretary of State certifies to be that person's release date within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act (in any case where there is such a release date); or
-- src:421 | (b) being detained under—
-- src:422 | (i) section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction), or
-- src:423 | (ii) section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder).
@ref reg 19(4) (src:417-423)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(4) — the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` person day MEANS
    `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`)
            AND (CONSIDER person's `release date that the Secretary of State certifies, within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST release THEN day LESS THAN release)
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995`)
            OR (person's `the person is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`)

-- (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply during the first 6 months when the person is a prisoner where (a) they were entitled to universal
-- credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner and the calculation of their award included an amount for the
-- housing costs element, and (b) they have not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond those 6 months.
-- The 6 months beginning with the day the person became a prisoner end the day before the same day 6 months on (fork F-6-MONTHS).
-- src:413 | (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply during the first 6 months when the person is a prisoner where—
-- src:414 | (a) the person was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner, and the calculation of their award included an amount for the housing costs element; and
-- src:415 | (b) the person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months.
@ref reg 19(2) (src:413-415)
GIVEN `day on which the person became a prisoner` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the person was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calculation of that award included an amount for the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(2) — paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` `day on which the person became a prisoner` day `the person was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner` `the calculation of that award included an amount for the housing costs element` `the person has been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` MEANS
    `within the first 6 months`
    AND (`the person was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner`)
    AND (`the calculation of that award included an amount for the housing costs element`)
    AND (NOT `the person has been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months`)
    WHERE
        `within the first 6 months` MEANS
            (day AT LEAST `day on which the person became a prisoner`)
            AND (day AT MOST ((`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `day on which the person became a prisoner` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months)) MINUS 1))

-- (1) Entitlement does not arise where a person is (a) a member of a religious order fully maintained by their order; (b) a prisoner
-- (except as paragraph (2) provides); or (c) serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital.
-- src:409 | (1) Entitlement to universal credit does not arise where a person is—
-- src:410 | (a) a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by their order;
-- src:411 | (b) a prisoner; or
-- src:412 | (c) serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital.
@ref reg 19(1) (src:409-412)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by their order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(b) does not apply under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(1) — entitlement does not arise` `the person is a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by their order` `the person is a prisoner` `paragraph (1)(b) does not apply under paragraph (2)` `the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` MEANS
    (`the person is a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by their order`)
    OR `a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) does not apply`
    OR (`the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital`)
    WHERE
        `a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) does not apply` MEANS
            (`the person is a prisoner`)
            AND (NOT `paragraph (1)(b) does not apply under paragraph (2)`)

-- (3) In the case of a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies, an award is not to include any element other than the housing costs
-- element.
-- src:416 | (3) In the case of a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies, an award of universal credit is not to include any element other than the housing costs element.
@ref reg 19(3) (src:416)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of an award`
      `the person is a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) — the award may include the element` element `the person is a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `the person is a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies`
    THEN element EQUALS `housing costs element`
    ELSE TRUE
